<section id="takeaways" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="takeaways">Takeaways</h2>
<ul>
<li>Demand more than triples between the early-morning low and the late-afternoon peak.</li>
<li>Response times stretch during the busiest hours, which is exactly when more residents are calling.</li>
<li>This is a starting point. Next steps are breaking it down by station, by call type, and by which segment of the response (call processing, turnout, or travel) is driving the delay.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="try-it-with-your-own-data" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="try-it-with-your-own-data">Try it with your own data</h2>
<p>Replace the simulation with your CAD export. You need at least a call-received timestamp and an arrival timestamp:</p>
